{"ts": 0.204073, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mWhere this lives for real\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThe prompt went back because each screen starts a fresh shell. A real\r\nterminal reads one file when it starts, and settings there last:\r\n", "len": 177}
{"ts": 0.204089, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n  ~/.bashrc     if your login shell is bash\r\n  ~/.zshrc      if it is zsh\r\n  ~/.bash_profile   on macOS with bash\r\n\r\nA line like  \u001b[92mPS1='me> '\u001b[0m  in that file gives you your own prompt every\r\ntime. Edit it in a normal terminal, not here; the tutor never touches it.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m for the task.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 326}
{"ts": 0.20767, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
{"ts": 0.207955, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 253}
{"ts": 0.223443, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[?2004hshelltutor> ", "len": 20}
